`,c.jsx(i.p,{children:"With the automotive industry shifting towards Zonal Architecture, in-vehicle networks have become exponentially complex. However, existing monitoring tools relied heavily on text-based logs, which lacked spatial context."}),`
`,c.jsx(i.p,{children:"Engineers had to mentally map abstract error codes to physical locations, leading to high cognitive load and delayed diagnosis. The disconnection between digital data and physical reality was a major bottleneck in the maintenance workflow."}),`
`,c.jsx("br",{}),`
`,c.jsx(i.h2,{children:"What is Zonal Architecture?"}),`
`,c.jsx(i.p,{children:"Zonal architecture is a modern automotive design that organizes a vehicle's electronics by physical location (zones like front-left, rear-right) instead of by function, using fewer, powerful zonal controllers to manage nearby sensors and actuators"}),`
